DEI Tech ("Licensor") hereby grants you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free license to download, install, and execute the official binary executable version of the software ("Software") on any computers, workstations, or Windows PE (Preinstallation Environment) maintenance media under your possession or control.
You are permitted to use this Software to service, diagnose, troubleshoot, and repair computer systems for commercial clients or end users without paying additional licensing fees, provided that no separate fee is charged for the Software itself.

2. DISTRIBUTION
You may freely redistribute exact, unmodified copies of the original binary package of the Software, provided that:
(a) No fee, payment, or consideration is charged for the Software (whether standalone or bundled with paid hardware, paid software, or commercial repair services);
(b) All copyright notices, trademarks, and branding belonging to Licensor remain intact and unmodified;
(c) This EULA is distributed along with the Software.

3. RESTRICTIONS
You shall not, and shall not permit any third party to:
(a) Sell, rent, lease, sublicense, loan, or otherwise monetize the Software itself (this does not restrict charging fees for your own repair, diagnostic, or consulting services performed using the Software, as permitted in Section 1);
(b) Decompile, reverse engineer, disassemble, decrypt, or otherwise attempt to derive or reconstruct the source code of the Software;
(c) Modify, alter, patch, translate, or create derivative works of the Software;
(d) Remove, obscure, or alter any proprietary notices, logos, or trademarks of Licensor;
(e) Bundle, inject, or repackage the Software with any adware, spyware, trojans, backdoors, or other malicious payloads.
Sections 3(b) and 3(c) apply to the Licensor's proprietary code only. They do not limit any rights you hold under the licenses of the third-party components included in the Software (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md), nor any right that cannot be excluded or limited by applicable law.

4. PRIVACY AND SECURITY
Licensor has not intentionally included any malware, spyware, backdoor, or trojan horse in the official binary release of the Software, and the Software does not collect personal identifiable information (PII) or telemetry.
Update check: by default, the Software periodically sends a single HTTPS request to the GitHub API (api.github.com) to check whether a newer release exists. The request carries no device identifier or personal data beyond what any network connection inherently reveals (such as your IP address, and the Software name and version in the User-Agent). You can turn this off in the Software's Settings. The Software never downloads or installs updates by itself; it only opens the official GitHub release page when you choose to.

5. DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTIES
THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. LICENSOR DOES NOT WARRANT THAT THE FUNCTIONS CONTAINED IN THE SOFTWARE WILL MEET YOUR REQUIREMENTS OR THAT THE OPERATION OF THE SOFTWARE WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED OR ERROR-FREE.

6. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY
TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL LICENSOR, ITS DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, OR AGENTS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES; LOSS OF USE, DATA, REVENUE, OR PROFITS; SYSTEM OR HARDWARE INSTABILITY; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE. USERS ASSUME ALL RISKS AND RESPONSIBILITIES FOR SYSTEM-LEVEL MODIFICATIONS.

